Amber, which some of the API tests are written in, on Kosmos: it chooses
what it calls by platform and stops at one it does not know, and Kosmos is
its POSIX one - all it asks of the platform is usleep, which the layer has.
And `<cctype>` where Amber calls isalnum, which glibc's headers bring in
without being asked and libc++'s do not.

diff -ruN a/external/amber/src/src/platform.h b/external/amber/src/src/platform.h
--- a/external/amber/src/src/platform.h	2026-11-19 15:39:07.238480057 -0300
+++ b/external/amber/src/src/platform.h	2026-11-19 15:39:07.238832335 -0300
@@ -33,6 +33,9 @@
 #elif defined(__QNX__)
 #define AMBER_PLATFORM_QNX 1
 #define AMBER_PLATFORM_POSIX 1
+#elif defined(__kosmos__)
+// Kosmos: the POSIX layer inside the process (`design.md` section 17).
+#define AMBER_PLATFORM_POSIX 1
 #else
 #error "Unknown platform."
 #endif
